# Security Baseline

Applies to every change that touches input, auth, storage, or the network.

- No hardcoded secrets. All secrets from env vars; presence validated at startup.
- All user input validated with a schema (zod, pydantic) at the boundary.
- SQL uses parameterized queries — never string interpolation.
- HTML output escaped; no `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` without sanitization.
- Auth AND authorization check on every protected endpoint (not just UI).
- Rate limiting on public endpoints (auth, search, writes).
- Error responses do not leak stack traces or internal paths in production.
- `.env`, `.env.local`, credentials in `.gitignore`.
- CORS restrictive — no `*` for credentialed endpoints.

## If a secret leaks
Rotate → invalidate derived tokens → scrub history (after rotation; scrubbing alone is not mitigation).
